## What

Makes Validate's `summary` fail when lanes are cancelled or time out. Makes the release publisher wait for a green Validate run on the exact tagged SHA. Makes `scripts/retag-release.sh` push main before it changes any tag or release.

- `.github/workflows/validate.yml`: the `summary` step reads `toJson(needs)` from env, prints every lane, and fails on any result other than success or skipped. It also fails on any skipped lane in a full run (release tag, merge queue, manual dispatch). `workflow_dispatch` now forces a full run, and `changes` exposes that as `full`. The bats path filter also covers `workflows/**` and `tests/fixtures/**`. The header comment is rewritten and the stale skill-gates comment block is removed. `summary.needs` is unchanged.
- `.github/workflows/release.yml`: a new `validate-verdict` job (read-only contents, actions and checks permissions, no soft-fail) runs `scripts/verify-release-ci.sh` for the tag. `publish` needs that job and requires its success. `checks: read` lets `gh run watch` read check-run annotations instead of getting a 403 on every poll (from the fresh read's optional notes).
- `scripts/retag-release.sh`: "Pushing main" now runs straight after the preconditions.
- `docs/CI-CD.md`: the validate.yml row now reads "Pull-request merge gate (`summary`) and exact-SHA release prerequisite", and the "no workflow writes a Validate verdict" line now says the `validate-verdict` job only reads the exact-SHA CI result.

## Why

- The summary step failed only on `failure`, so runs with cancelled lanes still reported a green `summary` (production cases 0cb418dd4, a4bf50952, 6d037f66c).
- Publish needed only the doc-release gate and pre-publish evidence, so v3.1.0 and v3.2.0 shipped from SHAs whose Validate run was red. The tested `scripts/verify-release-ci.sh` had no caller.
- The retag script deleted the GitHub release and the remote tag before pushing main. When main was rejected, the release was gone, and a rerun exited with "nothing to retag".
- Manual Validate runs were path-filtered. `verify-release-ci.sh` takes the newest run of any event for a SHA, so a manual run could stand in as a partial verdict.

Owner follow-ups:
- Enable admin enforcement on main after this merges (the retag reorder had to land first).
- Deferred, with revisit triggers: push:main or a scheduled full run (if a landed tree differs from a validated PR head, or direct pushes without a dispatch happen more than monthly); a Validate pre-check in retag (if a retag ends with the release deleted and nothing republished); an idempotency guard on the remote tag.
- Residual, outside this diff: `verify-release-ci.sh` picks the newest Validate run of any event for the SHA. A path-filtered pull_request run could only be chosen if the tagged commit is itself a PR head (a non-squash landing).

## How I tested

- `bats tests/scripts/validate-release-tag-full-ci.bats tests/scripts/release-workflow.bats tests/scripts/retag-release.bats tests/scripts/verify-release-ci.bats tests/scripts/test-bats-path-filter-wiring.bats`: 34/34 ok.
- New cases (12). The summary and Detect cases pull the shipped step shell out of the workflow with `yaml.safe_load`, assert it contains no `${{`, and run it with fixture `NEEDS_JSON`, `GITHUB_REF` and `GITHUB_EVENT_NAME`:
  - summary: cancelled lanes, a failed lane, a timed-out lane, path-filter skips on a PR, a skip on a tag, a fully green tag, a skip on a manual run;
  - Detect: workflow_dispatch writes `release=true` and pull_request writes `release=false`;
  - YAML structure;
  - bats filter globs;
  - `validate-verdict` wiring;
  - retag against a bare remote whose pre-receive hook rejects main, then a rerun after the hook is removed.
- Red proofs, on unfixed code:
  - summary cases: `AssertionError: summary/Check results: run text interpolates an expression`;
  - Detect: the `release=true` grep failed;
  - structure: `KeyError: 'full'`;
  - release: `AssertionError: ['doc-release-gate', 'pre-publish-evidence']`;
  - retag: `retag-release.bats line 161 [ "$status" -eq 1 ] failed` (the gh log already held `release delete`);
  - path filter: `AssertionError: ['**/*.bats']`.
- Red proofs by clause revert, in a scratch copy:
  - failure-only result check: cancelled and timed_out cases go red;
  - not_ok ignored at exit: failure, cancelled and timed_out cases go red;
  - skips failing regardless of `full`: the PR-skip case goes red;
  - full-run skip clause dropped: the tag and manual-run cases go red;
  - Detect without workflow_dispatch: red;
  - `full` output dropped, skill-gates comment restored or `branches: [main]` added: the structure case goes red;
  - either bats glob dropped: red;
  - `validate-verdict` dropped from needs or from if, `actions: read` dropped, or the verify call removed: red;
  - continue-on-error added: the soft-fail case goes red;
  - push main moved back after the deletions: the retag case goes red.
- `python3 -c 'import yaml,sys; ...' validate.yml release.yml`: rc 0.
- `bash scripts/regen-all.sh` then `--check`: "All generated projections are current."
- `ao gate check`: 47/47 pass. `ao gate check --full --workflow-coverage --require-workflow-parity`: 66/66 pass (with gocyclo v0.6.0 on PATH). ci.policy-parity passes, and no blocking workflow scripts are missing. The validate.yml script-coverage `comm` invariant is empty.
- CI bats command `bats --jobs 4 --no-parallelize-within-files --print-output-on-failure tests/scripts/*.bats`: 1400 tests, 12 failures, the same count as the local container baseline (root user and container process handling). The one difference, `a schema-valid skill passes`, passes 3/3 when its file runs alone.
- `bash tests/run-all.sh` (codex stub on PATH): 9 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped.
- `shellcheck scripts/retag-release.sh`: clean. `scripts/check-gate-tightening-ratchet.sh`: PASS.
- Fresh read (one author-distinct reader, one round, no re-run of checks). Question: "Can any path through the changed summary step, the validate-verdict job or the reordered retag script let a SHA whose exact Validate run did not fully succeed be merged or published, or delete a published release before main is pushed?" Verdict: PASS, no defects.

Observed on GitHub before merge: the run on superseded head dd7d4dbf4 was cancelled by the next push, and its `summary` failed with `❌ Some checks did not succeed (failure, cancelled or timed out)` listing the three cancelled lanes (job 119081440210). With main's current `summary` that run would have reported green.

Not checked:
- The next v* tag publishing only after `validate-verdict` prints `GO release-ci` (observable only on the next release).
- Go build/vet/test and go-lint (no Go changes).

